  "slug": "mitochondrial-resource-16ed",
  "summary": "New preprints pair selection-bias correction, survival pseudo-observations and uniform meta-analysis with cross-species genetic resources for interpreting association signals.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is making association estimates interpretable. One review covers ten methods for detecting and correcting selection bias in GWAS, organized by selection type and data availability, with an R repository. A rhesus macaque study uses restricted-mean survival pseudo-observations to connect exome variants to fibrosis and longevity. A uniform re-analysis of 1,037 public exercise omics contrasts applies random-effects meta-analysis across humans and rodents. The oyster assembly with GWAS and k-mer analysis, and the SheepGTEx pilot linking regulatory variants to 34 traits, are mainly resource-building across non-human species rather than bias-focused work. What is new is the explicit emphasis on bias correction, alternative outcome encodings and harmonized re-analysis, although only some items address robustness directly.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-14"
}
